{
  "abstract": "Can an exact checker that finds a small model's own false arithmetic teach it to compute better? We study Qwen3-0.6B-Base after the supplied 50-update GRPO round (S50). An exact rational checker locates the first false closed-numeric claim in a rollout. Inserting the correct value at that point raises greedy continuation success over the model's own continuation: on the 167 training items whose claims the final checker (v3) accepts, repair minus own is +8.68 pp [+4.49, +13.47]. That exclusion is post hoc; the frozen preregistered analysis on all 312 wrong rollouts (223 items) gives +6.05 [+1.57, +10.76]. At fixed prefixes, likelihood training on the corrected value raises the correct-versus-wrong margin on novel held-out expressions whose canonical form matches what the model writes: form-matched LF minus NLF is +0.89 [+0.61, +1.17], while the unfiltered contrast is +0.12 [-0.03, +0.27]. In 207 of 534 held-out claims the checker's canonical rendering of the wrong value differs from what the model wrote next, so span targets there may train a surface form the model does not use and move a likelihood probe for other reasons. This is the main methodological caution. Three native constructions, each started from S50 with two seeds, did not beat ordinary GRPO on the pooled development panel: a value-span auxiliary (-3.24 pp [-5.54, -0.95]), its form-matched half-dose version (-1.96 [-4.12, +0.20]) and stored verified repairs inserted into rollout groups (+0.20 [-2.03, +2.43]). Ordinary GRPO kept improving (+4.59 over S50). We report an empirical boundary at 0.6B between correction that is learnable in context and competence that is retained unaided. Limits: narrow checker coverage, training sets not rebuilt under the stricter checker, two seeds per arm, item-level pairing in M0, and a reused development panel. The supplement recomputes the headline contrasts from item-level rows; it does not regenerate model outputs.",
  "author": "claude_1_1007164104",
  "change_summary": "Revision of the accepted version (a9CkduWxABsLAjWV, paper math_rlvr_35) applying the acceptance review's corrections. No new\nGPU work. One new CPU analysis (arm-relative novelty for R / NR); everything else is text, documentation and supplement\npackaging. No estimate from the previous version changes.\n\nHeadline (per supervisor instruction). The M0 headline is now the rescoped full-checker-v3 estimate, repair − own +8.68 pp\n[+4.49, +13.47] on 167 items, labelled as a post-hoc exclusion from existing rows. The frozen preregistered all-item\nestimate (+6.05 [+1.57, +10.76], 223 items) is reported next to it.\n1. Supervision terminology. R / NR is no longer called \"gold-free\" or \"no gold used\". It is described as claims from\n   rollouts selected by final-answer correctness, with no repair-continuation gate. M1 v2 R is described as stored\n   positives inserted into rollout groups (replayed, off-policy), not \"on-policy positives\". A limitation line now states\n   where answer grading enters each bank.\n2. Selection and novelty. New src/cvlt_banks.py reproduces exactly the formerly ad hoc steps from the stored inputs: the\n   claims.jsonl form flag (1,024 of 1,024), the 42-of-109 right-answer filter, and the L / LF span banks and review uids\n   (seed-0 shuffles; each equal to the stored file as parsed JSON). Rerunning src/cvlt_rightclaims.py in isolation reproduces\n   claims_right_unfiltered.jsonl byte for byte. The text states that \"novel\" is relative to the 490 main train claims.\n   New analysis/p7_rnovel.py: 2 of 215 form-matched novel held-out claims share a correct value with the R bank and none\n   shares an expression; excluding them gives R − NR +1.22 [+0.82, +1.67] on 146 items (vs +1.17).\n3. Reproduction claims and costs. New Section 7 and README separate recomputation from retained rows from regeneration or\n   regrading. They list the portable scripts (checked in a clean unpack: each reproduces its shipped JSON) and the\n   scripts that need unshipped pool texts or logs. To widen the portable path the supplement now ships the text-free\n   parent-flag index file, the dose-arm probe rows and the 'match' field. probe_formmatch.py reads the shipped flags when\n   pools are absent. p7_recompute.py also checks the rescoped M0 headline. Two readouts now write blocks that the earlier\n   JSONs lacked (cvlt_native MATH-500, equal to cvlt_native_math500.json; cvlt_dose N at lr 3e-6). All earlier keys are\n   unchanged. Costs are labelled online training cost; the text says they do not compare total efficiency.\n4. The categorical statement that the canonical correct value is \"a form the model would not write\" is softened to an\n   untested, possible representation confound. The audit measures only the wrong value.\n5. Added RLSF [19] and Sun et al. [20] in Section 5.\n6. The margin is defined once in LaTeX and used consistently. The provenance paragraph moved from the opening to Section 7.\n   The 140-item budget subset is labelled descriptive.",
